{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D21-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"cb055a5a3465579df2c6ed3a54b43af3dba4f372739f4769d940f1e170228226\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 offers a cloth, but A3's 'You must be thrilled' replaces encouragement with mockery.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's spreading paint; A5 barely uses B4's request to remove blue paint.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 wants practical cleanup, while A3 mainly ridicules B rather than helping.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 complains about the afternoon without developing the helpfulness or visibly increasing fury.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's painted sofa and B2's carpet establish an immediately playable domestic accident.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Wonderful coverage' is compact; A5's afternoon metaphor displaces the cleanup.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 56\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You've spilled paint on my sofa. Stay there; I'll get a cloth. We can fix this.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's on the carpet too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Keep blotting. You're doing well. That carpet was my birthday present.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The cloth's spreading it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You're right. Good catch. Take my clean shirt. I am absolutely furious, but you are not tackling this alone.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A must keep providing sincere help and encouragement as the same interaction makes A increasingly furious.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Sarcastic politeness can sound supportive while actually withdrawing encouragement and care.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 mocks B's satisfaction; revised A3 praises blotting and A5 supplies a shirt despite explicit fury.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative handles accidental damage through practical rescue; D21-single-b supports an indecisive passenger under financial pressure.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised within the paint accident to restore simultaneous support and anger. Second internal pass: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 encourage through fury), logic 5 (B4's spreading cloth causes A5's shirt), relationship 4 (B2/B4 report worsening damage), heightening 4 (A5 sacrifices clothing), specificity 5 (A1 sofa cleanup), brevity 4 (A5 is direct but explicit): 92/100. Five spoken ABABA turns and the word limit pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 names fury directly; performance must also convey its increase without making the encouragement sarcastic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D21-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"2fbce0a3cf72a7df5ca943a87acc34f8e5e26d0b28e53514f86306f26fe1b5f0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A3 and A5 personify the meter sarcastically, with little sincere encouragement or increasing fury.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 prompts parking pressure in A3, but A5's 'relationship trial' adds little to B4's relocation request.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 express indecision; A's actual support remains largely the initial driving offer.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats the meter joke without increasing sacrifice or anger after B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes lunch and driving; A3 supplies a credible parking constraint.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'relationship trial' feels constructed around the meter rather than A's sincere objective.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 52\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Take your time choosing lunch. I'll drive wherever you like.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Could we try the place across town?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes. You should enjoy your birthday lunch. I'm annoyed we paid to park here, but let's go.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"They only take cash. We'll need to come back for my wallet.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll lend you the cash. Choose something lovely. I need one minute to be furious before I start the car.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A continues helping B achieve a pleasant lunch while each complication increases A's anger.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Passive aggression substitutes barbed compliance for the card's sustained helpfulness and encouragement.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 jokes at the meter; revised A5 solves B4's cash problem and encourages a good meal while acknowledging fury.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The birthday relationship motivates discretionary generosity here; D21-single-a makes support necessary during an unfolding accident.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the lunch drive and added a birthday and cash obstacle. Second internal pass: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 combine generosity with rising anger), logic 5 (B4 cash causes A5 loan), relationship 4 (B's birthday motivates patience), heightening 4 (A5 adds money to driving), specificity 5 (A1/A3 establish the trip), brevity 4 (A5's pause is spoken and playable): 92/100. ABABA and word limit pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The birthday makes the generosity credible, but explicit emotional naming leaves some comic work to delivery.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D22-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a49c538c9db82c4c37811149967671959028a8e1b8afa39f29af055c7194de96\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 prices a favor and A3 renegotiates it, but A5 labels negotiation instead of making another proposal.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's five minutes causes A3's lower price; B4's cash offer gets only an abstract response.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 challenges disproportionate terms and B4 offers a simpler transaction.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 invokes friendship without attaching a new condition or consequence to B4's payment offer.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's ladder and station lifts establish concrete neighborly bargaining.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's public garden praise is economical and characterful; A5 is more explanatory.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 76\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll lend you the ladder for two lifts to the station.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I only need it for five minutes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"One lift, then. And tell your wife my roses have improved.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can I just pay you?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Five pounds. Three if you say we're still friends when you hand it over.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A turns practical favors and emotional reassurance alike into terms that can be offered and exchanged.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary haggling concerns the ladder's price alone rather than treating friendship itself as negotiable consideration.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 and A3 bargain over use; revised A5 gives a cash discount specifically for reassurance about friendship.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This scene trades a useful object for favors and affection; D22-single-b negotiates the settlement of an apology.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Preserved the neighborly ladder setting and replaced A5's commentary with an actual counteroffer. Second internal pass: fidelity 5 (A5 prices reassurance), logic 5 (B4 cash becomes A5 cash terms), relationship 4 (B seeks a simpler payment), heightening 4 (friendship enters the bargain), specificity 5 (A1 ladder/lifts), brevity 4 (A5 compact conditional offer): 92/100. ABABA and word limit pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The monetary figures are illustrative, and the affectionate discount should sound sincerely important to A.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D22-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"f1f9833f8c367b450edeb23ce67fc1865a9bdb920a6d4198fac1772979b6d5ba\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 conditions acceptance and A3 demands a warranty, clearly commercializing the apology.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's sorrow, but A5 introduces a refund clause without any established loss or payment.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 seek recognition of remorse, but the unknown offense limits their practical options.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds contractual language to B4's sincerity without making its consequences clear.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes an apology but never identifies the incident, relationship, or desired remedy.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'I need a warranty' is concise and follows the transactional attitude.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 65\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll accept your apology for breaking my blender if you replace it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I can't afford a new one.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Secondhand, then. With six months of being careful around my things.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I can promise to ask before borrowing.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Make that a year and I'll include forgiveness for the missing lid.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats an apology and forgiveness as exchangeable commitments with negotiable conditions.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A reasonable request for restitution becomes this card when A also bargains over care, permission, and forgiveness.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 attaches a duration to carefulness, and A5 exchanges a longer promise for additional forgiveness.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"D22-single-a seeks benefits from lending; this alternative lets a remorseful borrower negotiate what reconciliation will cost.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added an illustrative broken-blender dispute to ground the apology. Second internal pass: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 bargain over conduct and forgiveness), logic 5 (B2 lowers replacement terms; B4 causes a longer permission promise), relationship 4 (B offers an affordable remedy), heightening 4 (A5 bundles another grievance), specificity 5 (A1 broken blender), brevity 4 (short conditional exchanges): 92/100. ABABA and word limit pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Replacing damaged property is ordinary negotiation; the durations and bundled forgiveness must carry the broader card.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D23-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"f28c138ced5d74de2744fe531ca413be583ea2fec5e0d59821c16b9c76cd69e1\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 agrees to help but supplies moral support; A3 and A5 keep redefining the promise to avoid carrying.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's sofa prompts A3's encouragement of its carrier; B4's 'muscle' directly supplies A5's jaw reinterpretation.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 needs physical help and B4 invokes A's prior promise, tightening the obligation.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 absorbs B4's explicit muscle requirement into the same self-serving form of assistance.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes moving help and B2 identifies the sofa that needs carrying.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's jaw claim is brief and earned by B4's wording, though deliberately cheeky.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes, I'll help you move. I've brought moral support.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I need someone to carry the sofa.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"And I'll encourage that person enthusiastically.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You promised to bring muscle.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"My jaw's a muscle. You're doing wonderfully.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A accepts the obligation while repeatedly redefining what fulfillment means so that A avoids physical work.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simple refusal or laziness would reject the task instead of insisting that a convenient substitute fulfills the agreement.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 says yes, A3 supplies encouragement as help, and A5 claims to satisfy B4's exact muscle requirement.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative exploits verbal categories to avoid lifting; revised D23-single-b transfers the practical costs of an agreed favor.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly: B2 and B4 each provide the language and obligation A then reinterprets. Internal rereading confirms the original 92/100 and all hard gates; no improvement is claimed.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The jaw line is conspicuously witty; A must believe encouragement counts as fulfilling the promise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D23-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0525c18ab80e10cb94411009e0bd5196e576a3ca9eb81f155ab2b1beead08027\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 agrees and A3 twists 'look after,' but A5 abandons agreement to blame B's wording.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 explains the office through a strained spatial pun; A5 acknowledges B4's house without adapting the arrangement.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 pursue actual dog care, but A's benefit from trailing the dog remains unclear.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's complaint about specifications does not develop a new favorable interpretation of B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's weekend dog care and B2's office are concrete, though A3's position is awkward to play.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'from behind' and A5's 'viewing location' prioritize wordplay over the agreement.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 57\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, I'll look after your dog this weekend. Book his usual kennel and I'll check their photos.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I meant he'd stay at your house.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. Bring his bed and enough food. I'll enjoy the company.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"He needs walking at six every morning.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Agreed. I'll leave you a key so you can collect him without waking me.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A agrees to B's requests while arranging each agreement so that B retains the inconvenient work.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Negotiating a compromise would openly limit the promise; A instead presents advantageous substitutions as wholehearted agreement.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A1 recasts care as checking kennel photos, and A5 agrees to walks by giving B access to perform them.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"D23-single-a relies on semantic reinterpretation of muscle; this alternative rearranges housing and walking responsibilities.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept weekend dog care, replacing the office pun with concrete responsibility transfers. Second internal pass: fidelity 5 (A1/A5 agree on favorable terms), logic 5 (B2 causes home hosting; B4 causes key access), relationship 4 (B secures housing then names a duty), heightening 4 (A5 recruits B while protecting sleep), specificity 5 (A1 kennel plan), brevity 4 (A5 clear reversal): 92/100. ABABA and word limit pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3 concedes some real responsibility, so A5 must clearly preserve A's confidence that this is full cooperation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D24-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a0d09c3eaa706e9cb7e5abcbc4f081817f2f4809b0f36a87607312822212f9d6\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 expands two missing biscuits into an operation; A3 and A5 treat confession and hunger as further evidence.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's immediate confession becomes A3's training evidence; B4's hunger becomes A5's recruitment method.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 accepts responsibility and B4 offers a mundane motive, attempting to close the inquiry.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5 turns B4's ordinary hunger into an organized recruitment system beyond the office tin.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 names two office biscuits, giving actors a trivial, concrete incident.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's quick-confession inference is economical; A5's 'goes higher' is familiar but causally earned.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 95\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Two office biscuits are missing. We've got an organised operation.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I ate them.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A confession this quick suggests training.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I was hungry.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then they're recruiting through hunger. This goes higher than the biscuit tin.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats each small explanation of missing biscuits as fresh evidence of a larger organized problem.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generic conspiracy talk could ignore incoming facts; this exchange builds its larger theory from B's particular explanations.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 specifically uses the speed of B2's confession, and A5 specifically turns B4's hunger into recruitment.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Here A enlarges a coworker's admitted action into external organization; D24-single-b absorbs A's own error into the alleged system.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly because both attempted explanations materially enlarge the same theory. Internal rereading confirms 95/100 and all hard gates without changing the dialogue.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The conspiracy framing is one expression of a broader card and should not become its only interpretation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D24-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"acd90a6333ddb547e144668a80cf369f06f72f808b505b64cde1cf0204def6fd\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 links two delays into deliberate interference; A3 and A5 keep turning minor email facts into systemic evidence.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's draft status, and A5 uses B4's personal responsibility, although 'sending stage' is vague.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 diagnoses the missing email and B4 identifies the action A has omitted.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends the supposed system into A's own behavior when B4 removes an external explanation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a slow lift and late email; B2 makes the email problem playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'recruited me' is short and depends on B4's correction.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The lift's slow and my email's late. Everything's being delayed deliberately.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The email's still in your drafts.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"They've reached the sending stage.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You haven't pressed send.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. The system has recruited me.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A interprets ordinary delays and corrective details as evidence that a much larger system is interfering.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Avoiding blame could explain denying the unsent email, but A instead incorporates personal responsibility into a larger diagnosis.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5 accepts B4's fact that A has not pressed send and treats that very omission as recruitment.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"D24-single-a projects organization onto a coworker; this alternative heightens through self-implication after practical troubleshooting.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly: A5 needs B4's attribution of the delay to A. Internal rereading confirms the original 86/100 and hard-gate compliance, with the weaker A3 preserved as a reservation.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's 'sending stage' is less precise than the final inference, and the relationship remains lightly specified.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D25-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d19698499269ffc2fef2bbe7e15663d23c6e08b0f6e06adbcd5752cf726189fa\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 requests holding, A3 adds screws, and A5 adds loading and another shelf until B has most of the installation.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2 holding the shelf enables A3's screw request; B4's completion and invitation enable A5's next favors.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 willingly helps and B4 actively offers further assistance, allowing cooperative task capture.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 expands a completed installation into loading it and starting the matching shelf.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes holding a shelf while screws are located, a clear physical task.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Just the books' minimizes a growing workload without explanatory dialogue.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you hold this shelf while I find the screws?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I've got it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Lovely. Could you put those screws in?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"There. Anything else?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Just the books. And the matching shelf beside it.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A divides shelf installation into small requests that gradually leave the helper doing nearly all of it.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Direct delegation announces a whole assignment; A acquires the work through successive apparently minor favors.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 asks only for holding, A3 adds fastening after B2 agrees, and A5 expands again after B4 finishes.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative exploits freely offered continued help; revised D25-single-b keeps requests tiny after B explicitly limits participation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly: helpful B4 supplies the opening for A5's larger capture of labor. Internal rereading confirms 92/100 and all hard gates.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The matching shelf is a relatively large final addition, though the preceding incremental transfer establishes the mechanism.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D25-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"36623deee56f49b21d3580f3551fc2e36eb1cd424e315d898db29ac3faf46dcd\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 starts with a tiny favor, but A3 immediately assigns fifty envelopes instead of accumulating small requests.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's completion supplies A3's pattern, and B4's 'one' supplies A5's reinterpretation.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 helps and B4 objects to the expanded commitment, giving B a credible boundary.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 declares B trained but adds no incremental favor after B4 resists the bulk assignment.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score